// cl: /DNDEBUG /DWIN32 /MD /EHsc
// partial score=0.973 date=2026-09-29
// ?doForceObjectSelection@ScriptActions@@IAEXABVAsciiString@@0_N0@Z
//
// Retail body at 0x002FAF10 (481 bytes, ends RET 16 at 0x002FB0EE).
//
// Identity: the matched caller ScriptActions::executeAction reaches this
// body through the OBJECT_FORCE_SELECT arm; the EA source file is
// GameEngine/Source/GameLogic/ScriptEngine/ScriptActions.cpp and the
// declared arity (AsciiString const&, AsciiString const&, bool, AsciiString
// const&, __thiscall, RET 16) is exactly what the bytes witness.
//
// The Zero Hour twin in the same file cannot hold this body: BFME takes the
// team name BY VALUE through ScriptEngine vtable +0x44, walks the team member
// list with the virtual-base-adjusted Object DLINK pointer-to-member, and
// replaces Zero Hour's unconditional deselectAllDrawables with a
// controlling-player gate around a 0x3E9 GameMessage plus the +0xE0
// InGameUI select slot.  This TU therefore keeps every facade local, the
// idiom the landed ScriptActions_doTeamUseCommandButtonOnNearestEnemy.cpp and
// Rva002F7820.cpp siblings use.
//
// STATE: probe reports size ours=481 retail=481 with 13 differing non-reloc
// bytes and shape 0.993 -- ONE instruction out of position.  Everything from
// +0x30 (the AsciiString copy ctor) through the whole loop body (+0x67..+0xC7),
// the controlling-player gate, the 0x3E9 GameMessage block, the 0x70-byte
// AudioEventRTS block and the InGameUI +0xE0 select block, the +0x38/+0x40/
// +0x3C camera Coord3D copy in retail's x,z,y order, and the whole EH
// prologue/epilogue with sub esp,0x8c / add esp,0x98 is BYTE-IDENTICAL to
// retail.  Earlier sessions that reported the camera load order or the EBX/EDI
// allocation as unreproducible were wrong: both are reproduced here (see the
// four spelling levers noted on the body below).
//
// RESIDUE (the only one left, 13 bytes, 2026-09-29 re-measured): the def's
// BASIC BLOCK and the EBX/EDI choice are one coupled decision, and the two
// settings trade against each other.  Retail's preheader is
//     mov esi,[eax+0xc] / xor ebx,ebx / mov ecx,0x401140 / mov edx,-100 /
//     xor edi,edi
// i.e. the `bestGuess = 0` xor sits at +0x4B (block 1, after the null-Team
// `je`), bestGuess holds EBX and the DLINK vbtable index holds EDI.  Two
// source shapes reach the two halves separately and neither both:
//   (a) `bestGuess = 0;` BEFORE `if (!team) return;` -- this file.  EBX/EDI
//       come out RIGHT (xor ebx,ebx at +0x40 for bestGuess, xor edi,edi at
//       +0x57 for the index) but MSVC 7.1 sinks the branch-independent
//       constant store to the top of the entry block, so the xor lands at
//       +0x40 instead of +0x4B.  13 differing bytes, shape 0.993.
//   (b) `Object *bestGuess = 0;` AFTER the guard -- the Zero Hour source
//       order at inputs/reference/CnC_Generals_Zero_Hour/.../ScriptActions.cpp
//       :4637.  The xor lands at +0x4B (right) but the allocator then gives
//       bestGuess EDI and the vbtable index EBX, swapping every later use:
//       16 differing bytes at +0x4C, +0x58, +0xA6, +0xAD, +0xB2, +0xB8, +0xCA,
//       +0xD2, +0xD4, +0xE9, +0x10F, +0x11F, +0x123, +0x184, +0x187, +0x18A.
// The def's live range therefore only out-prioritises the vbtable index for
// EBX while it starts in block 0; moving it into block 1 loses that priority.
// Shape (a) is the better of the two and is what this file keeps.
//
// MEASURED, all shape (b) unless noted, every one 481 B: def after the guard;
// braced `{ return; }` guard; `if (team == 0) return;`; initialised declaration
// after the guard; two and three defs around the guard; a def inside its own
// `{}`; a def through `(Object*)0`, a folding pointer subtraction, an inlined
// null helper, `slots[0]`, a struct field and a `bestGuess = 0 && team`
// fold -- all 16; a def in the for-init or for-condition comma -- 16; a
// `register` hint -- 16; DLINK_ITERATOR ctor body assigning m_getNext before
// m_cur and vice versa, ctor parameter order swapped, iterate_ returning the
// PMF first, an explicit copy ctor, advance() split into advanceOne(), done()
// as `0 == m_cur` and `!(m_cur != 0)`, cur() through a named local, extra
// references to bestGuess in the loop, `Object *&slot = bestGuess`, a named
// ObjectID temp and a named head local -- all 16.  Shape (a) variants: the
// same header and loop-body permutations, all 13.  `tools/eh_levers.py`
// (5 choices) reports only throw()/EHc spellings, `tools/shape_family_levers.py`
// over all ten families reports only the camera cam.x/cam.y swap, and a
// 9-choice / 17-alternative disjoint shape_search over the def block, the
// DLINK definition order, the loop-body references and the accessor spellings
// ran 6 trials with no improving output (best 0.9730 = this file unchanged).
// The two positions encode the same CFG, so the residue is a scheduler and
// register-priority artifact, not a semantic difference.  Body banked as a
// partial at 13 differing bytes; the naked __emit lift stays the only
// byte-matching coverage for this address.

